# The same family as on the clean side: `Source.read` runs one of the overrides of `Feed` and `Tape`, on the Source the
# caller calls it on. That `Feed.read` follows `Archive.read` and gives a str where `Source.read` promises bytes is
# `check`'s to ask; neither is a type of the code's, so the picture is the clean side's: what an override gives goes
# back to the dispatch that ran it.
route reading.feeds.Source
step Source()/Source.read
step Source()/Source.read/Feed.read
step Source()/Source.read/Tape.read

line entry > Source()/Source.read call
known #100 line Source > Source()/Source.read/Feed.read value
known #100 line Source > Source()/Source.read/Tape.read value
line Source()/Source.read/Feed.read > Source()/Source.read back
line Source()/Source.read/Tape.read > Source()/Source.read back

home Source Source()

side entry left

# each override takes a value of its own class from beyond, and the Source ends at the border of the dispatch
known #100 extra line Source > Source()/Source.read value
known #100 extra line Feed > Source()/Source.read/Feed.read value
known #100 extra line Tape > Source()/Source.read/Tape.read value
known #100 extra home Feed Source()
known #100 extra home Tape Source()
